\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Data flow of the adaptive scheme, from the base predictive to the upper prediction limit. The transport branch (left) estimates and regularises the map; the adaptive branch (right) maintains the effective miscoverage level. The two are coupled only through the transported calibration pool, and the order of operations within a date is stated at the top: the conformal quantile is taken at the level in force before the day's own error is observed, and that error is fed back only after the seven-day horizon embargo.}}{13}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:flow}{{4}{13}{Data flow of the adaptive scheme, from the base predictive to the upper prediction limit. The transport branch (left) estimates and regularises the map; the adaptive branch (right) maintains the effective miscoverage level. The two are coupled only through the transported calibration pool, and the order of operations within a date is stated at the top: the conformal quantile is taken at the level in force before the day's own error is observed, and that error is fed back only after the seven-day horizon embargo}{figure.4}{}}
